```ts
const ORANGE_HRM = "https://opensource-demo.orangehrmlive.com/web/index.php";
const { browser, page } = await launch();

await page.goto(ORANGE_HRM + "/auth/login");
await page.getByPlaceholder("Username").fill("Admin");
await page.getByPlaceholder("Password").fill("admin123");
await page.getByRole("button", { name: "Login" }).click();
await page.waitForURL("**/dashboard/index");

const lastName = "Verify" + Math.floor(Math.random() * 100000);
console.log("creating:", lastName);

await page.goto(ORANGE_HRM + "/pim/addEmployee");
await page.getByPlaceholder("First Name").fill("Temp");
await page.getByPlaceholder("Last Name").fill(lastName);
await page.getByRole("button", { name: "Save" }).click();
await page.waitForLoadState("networkidle");

// Find the row by what it SAYS, then step sideways to the actions cell.
await page.goto(ORANGE_HRM + "/pim/viewEmployeeList");
await page.getByPlaceholder("Type for hints...").first().fill(lastName);
await page.getByRole("button", { name: "Search" }).click();
await page.waitForLoadState("networkidle");

const actionsCell = page.locator(
  "xpath=//div[text()='" + lastName + "']/parent::div/following-sibling::div[last()]",
);
await actionsCell.locator("i.bi-trash").click();
await page.getByRole("button", { name: "Yes, Delete" }).click();

await show(page);
await browser.close();
```

**Why `parent::div` is in there.** The text node's immediate parent is an inner wrapper that has no siblings of its own, so stepping sideways from it finds nothing. Going up one more level reaches the real table cell, whose siblings are the other cells in that row. Dropping `parent::div` is the single most common way this expression silently matches zero elements.

**Why this beats a column index.** `following-sibling::div[last()]` says *"the last cell in this row"* — it keeps working when a column is added. `div[7]` does not.

> This is a live, shared sandbox. If someone else's data collides, a fresh `Math.random()` is the fix — which is exactly why the name is generated rather than fixed.

